<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/follows> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The `to` Element succeeds the `from` Element, establishing a unidirectional sequence. This succession is defined as chronological, procedural, or logical. It is used to represent either a temporal order (e.g., in a workflow) or a logical order for processing and traversal (e.g., in an ordered list)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Conducting controlled tests, experiments or simulations to verify that specific requirements regarding performance, functionality, robustness, etc. are met."@en .
